{"description":"The MCP tool list emitted annotations under non-standard keys: `readOnly`, `destructive`, `openWorld`. The MCP specification defines `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `idempotentHint`, `openWorldHint`. A client that reads the standard keys ignores unknown ones, so the approval prompts these annotations exist to drive were silently disabled for every tool. The existing test asserted the wrong keys, so the defect was locked in rather than caught.","impact":"An agent-facing safety signal that never reached any conforming client. Fix: emit the specification keys, add `idempotentHint`, keep `riskClass` alongside as this server's own richer classification, and assert both the presence of the standard keys and the absence of the old ones."}